{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_50","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"goai-litsearch","tool":"save_to_library","arguments":{"papers_json":"[{"id":"W3036550726","title":"Broad temperature dependence, high conductivity, and structure-property relations of cold sintering of LLZO-based composite electrolytes","authors":["Joo-Hwan Seo","Hiroto Nakaya","Yuki Takeuchi","Zhongming Fan","Hideaki Hikosaka","Ramakrishnan Rajagopalan","Enrique D. Gomez","Masato Iwasaki","Clive A. Randall"],"year":2020,"venue":"Journal of the European Ceramic Society","doi":"10.1016/j.jeurceramsoc.2020.06.050","arxiv_id":null,"url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jeurceramsoc.2020.06.050","pdf_url":"https://scholarsphere.psu.edu/resources/7e3cb16f-6f81-42cf-aa5d-a74e03bb24b9/downloads/20449","abstract":null,"citation_count":79,"publication_type":"article","sources":["openalex"]},{"id":"W3040795836","title":"Developing high safety Li-metal anodes for future high-energy Li-metal batteries: strategies and perspectives","authors":["Dai‐Huo Liu","Zhengyu Bai","Matthew Li","Aiping Yu","Dan Luo","Wenwen Liu","Lin Yang","Jun Lü","Khalil Amine","Zhongwei Chen"],"year":2020,"venue":"Chemical Society Reviews","doi":"10.1039/c9cs00636b","arxiv_id":null,"url":"https://doi.org/10.1039/c9cs00636b","pdf_url":"https://www.osti.gov/servlets/purl/1660542","abstract":"battery systems. However, the notorious Li-dendrite growth problem results in serious safety concerns for any energy storage application. Through a recent combination of interface-based science, nanotechnology-based solutions and characterization methods, the LMA is now primed for a technological boom. In this review, the recent emerging strategies and perspectives on LMAs are summarized, following which the current huge evolution in interfacial chemistry regulation, optimizing electrolyte components, designing a rational 'host' for lithium metal, optimizing \"solid-state electrolytes\" and other emerging strategies for developing high-safety LMAs is highlighted. Furthermore, several state-of-the-art in situ/operando synchrotron-based X-ray techniques for high safety LMB research are introduced. With the further development of LMAs in the future, subsequent application in high energy LMBs is to be expected.","citation_count":486,"publication_type":"article","sources":["openalex"]},{"id":"W4363651897","title":"Recent Progress in and Perspectives on Emerging Halide Superionic Conductors for All-Solid-State Batteries","authors":["Kaiyong Tuo","Chunwen Sun","Shuqin Liu"],"year":2023,"venue":"Electrochemical Energy Reviews","doi":"10.1007/s41918-023-00179-5","arxiv_id":null,"url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s41918-023-00179-5","pdf_url":"https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1007/s41918-023-00179-5.pdf","abstract":"Abstract Rechargeable all-solid-state batteries (ASSBs) are considered to be the next generation of devices for electrochemical energy storage. The development of solid-state electrolytes (SSEs) is one of the most crucial subjects in the field of energy storage chemistry. The newly emerging halide SSEs have recently been intensively studied for application in ASSBs due to their favorable combination of high ionic conductivity, exceptional chemical and electrochemical stability, and superior mechanical deformability. In this review, a critical overview of the development, synthesis, chemical stability and remaining challenges of halide SSEs is given. The design strategies for optimizing the ionic conductivity of halide SSEs, such as element substitution and crystal structure design, are summarized in detail. Moreover, the associated chemical stability issues in terms of solvent compatibility, humid air stability and corresponding degradation mechanisms are discussed. In particular, advanced in situ/operando characterization techniques applied to halide-based ASSBs are highlighted. In addition, a comprehensive understanding of the interface issues, cost issues, and scalable processin …[truncated]","cit